    decision:
      "Fixed a real money-integrity bug in refund.updated's reversal handler (src/app/api/stripe/webhook/route.ts, shipped 2026-07-19 in commerce-order-refund-reversal-tracking): it cleared refundedAt purely off the single refund event's own status (failed/canceled), with no re-check against the underlying charge. Stripe allows multiple independent (e.g. partial) refunds on one charge — if Refund A succeeds (setting refundedAt) and a later, separate Refund B on the SAME charge then fails, the old handler still cleared refundedAt unconditionally, silently re-admitting a genuinely-refunded order back into the 'owed to client' pool and turning off the payout-clawback flag despite real missing money. Fixed by re-fetching the charge (stripe.charges.retrieve, keyed by the refund's own `charge` field via new refundChargeId helper) and re-checking its own aggregate amount_refunded (chargeHasRefund — the exact predicate charge.refunded already uses) before clearing anything; only clears when the re-derived ground truth shows zero net refund remaining.",
